### Provisioning Upsert

Extend `admin.provisionChannel` subscriber handling so stable subscribers can be updated on rerun.

Desired behavior:

```text
same subscriber_key or derived subscriber ID + new config.filters
  update existing subscriber config_json and mutable presentation fields

same subscriber_key + same config
  reuse without meaningful changes
```

Mutable fields for provisioning upsert:

```text
name / display_name
config_json
enabled
external_resource_id
source_app / external_tenant_id / external_user_id inherited ownership fields
```

Destination changes need careful handling:

```text
webhook/slack destination change
  Can update after URL validation.

email destination change
  Prefer requiring a new subscriber_key, or force authorization back to pending if supported.
```

Recommendation for MVP:

```text
Support config/name/enabled updates for existing subscribers.
Do not silently change email destination for an existing subscriber_key in this story.
Return a validation error if email destination differs from the stored normalized destination.
```

`admin.createSubscriber` can remain create-or-reuse for backward compatibility. The upsert behavior can live inside `admin.provisionChannel` only, or a new internal helper such as `upsertProvisionedSubscriber`.

